WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:02.768
-Our first guest tonight
is an incredible actor

00:00:02.768 --> 00:00:05.472
who produced and stars in
the new movie "Without Remorse."

00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:08.475
It's available on
Amazon Prime Video tomorrow.

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:11.410
Here he is -- Michael B. Jordan!

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:14.580
That's what I'm talking about!
Yes!

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:16.649
Come on, bud!

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:19.518
It's always great to see you,
buddy. Welcome back to the show.

00:00:19.518 --> 00:00:22.155
-Man, thanks for having me, man.
Thanks for having me.

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:24.089
How is everybody doing?
-Everyone's doing good.

00:00:24.089 --> 00:00:25.558
We got a crowd.

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:27.793
We have people
back in the studio.

00:00:27.793 --> 00:00:29.328
It's awesome.

00:00:29.328 --> 00:00:31.664
-Love it. I love it.
-Pal, I want to ask you,

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:34.033
'cause the last time --
Since you've been on the show,

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:39.305
you were on the cover of a
magazine that was pretty epic.

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:41.607
Here it is right here.
The cover of "People."

00:00:41.607 --> 00:00:43.743
You're the Sexiest Man Alive.

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:45.144
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:45.144 --> 00:00:46.278
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:46.278 --> 00:00:48.681
-Now, I want to know --
I want to know,

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:53.653
how has your life changed since
being named Sexiest Man Alive?

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:56.655
-I mean, it's a gift
and a curse, you know?

00:00:56.655 --> 00:00:58.558
People don't tell you that

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:00.926
you instantly have a target
on your back.

00:01:00.926 --> 00:01:03.862
I mean, all my boys, you know,
in every group chat,

00:01:03.862 --> 00:01:06.699
just imagine -- they're just
constantly roasting me.

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:09.302
And it's like everything I do,
it's,

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:11.070
"Oh, it's because
the Sexiest Man Alive

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:12.238
is taking off his jacket.

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:13.840
Oh, look at the way
he wears his shirt.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.541
He eats like
the Sexiest Man Alive."

00:01:15.541 --> 00:01:17.543
It's like, "All right.
Enough is enough."

00:01:17.543 --> 00:01:20.680
But on the other hand,
my mom and, like, my aunts,

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:23.683
you know, they have it
kind of vacuum sealed.

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:26.152
You know what I mean? And, like,
you know, Saran-wrapped,

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:28.120
you know, that's, like,
up on the mantle.

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:31.424
-They bought every issue,
yeah, off the news stand.

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:33.226
-Every one.
Every one. Every one.
-That's awesome.

00:01:33.226 --> 00:01:34.427
See, come on, bud.

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:36.195
Here you are on another cover
of a magazine.

00:01:36.195 --> 00:01:39.165
This is the "Men's Health"
cover, which look at this.

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:41.234
Come on. That's...

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:44.336
-My boy Leo -- Leo Volcy --
did that cover.

00:01:44.336 --> 00:01:46.472
He's my photographer
and videographer.

00:01:46.472 --> 00:01:49.275
That was his first cover.
So it's special, it's special.

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:51.644
-Did he take this picture
on the inside of you --

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:55.081
This is you underwater
holding a rock.

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:57.584
-Yes. Yes,
he took that one, too.

00:01:57.584 --> 00:01:58.951
It was a crazy workout, man.

00:01:58.951 --> 00:02:00.820
I'm sitting up there, you know,
jumping up to the surface

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.121
trying to get some air,

00:02:02.121 --> 00:02:04.023
dropping down there
trying to get the perfect --

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:05.425
the framing right.

00:02:05.425 --> 00:02:07.593
-I'm sorry.
That's a workout?

00:02:07.593 --> 00:02:11.497
You go down, you find a rock,
and you carry it?

00:02:11.497 --> 00:02:15.100
-Yeah, well, a lot of surfers,
you know, and athletes,

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:17.102
they work on their breathing
and their conditioning,

00:02:17.102 --> 00:02:18.638
you know, underwater.

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:21.507
So you would carry a stone that
would weight you to the bottom,

00:02:21.507 --> 00:02:24.777
and you would just get
your cardio in underwater.

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:27.013
So, yeah, that was something
that we worked on.

00:02:27.013 --> 00:02:29.382
-We have a similar workout.

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:31.583
[ Both laugh ]

00:02:31.583 --> 00:02:33.319
-I'm sure, man.

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:35.521
-You're in pre-productive
for "Creed III."

00:02:35.521 --> 00:02:37.556
I am psyched about this.
I can't wait.

00:02:37.556 --> 00:02:40.326
I loved the first two.
But you're directing this one.

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:42.895
That's massive, buddy.
Congratulations.
-Yes.

00:02:42.895 --> 00:02:44.997
-That's big.
-Thank you so much, man.
Thank you, thank you.

00:02:44.997 --> 00:02:47.400
I'm really excited about it,
you know?

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:50.469
It's the one character and story
that I know the most.

00:02:50.469 --> 00:02:52.872
You know, third time doing it.

00:02:52.872 --> 00:02:55.608
It's the third time
I've played any role before.

00:02:55.608 --> 00:02:58.077
And I don't think you're ever
really ready to direct,

00:02:58.077 --> 00:03:01.848
but, you know, you've just
got to jump in the deep end

00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:03.883
and, you know, sink or swim.

00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:06.386
-I want to talk about
your new movie.

00:03:06.386 --> 00:03:08.420
But before that,
I just want to quickly mention

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:10.923
this cool thing you're doing
for your hometown,

00:03:10.923 --> 00:03:12.725
for Newark.
-Yeah.

00:03:12.725 --> 00:03:16.362
I'm putting on, you know,
HBCU Classic.

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:17.897
It's called
the Hoop Dreams Classic

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:20.132
that is taking place
in Newark, New Jersey,

00:03:20.132 --> 00:03:23.035
at the Prudential Center
December 18th.

00:03:23.035 --> 00:03:25.170
And I'm really excited about it,
man.

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:28.007
Honestly, just really
highlighting the HBCU's

00:03:28.007 --> 00:03:31.610
and putting them on a stage
so they can be recognized,

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:33.545
their talent, and bringing
the community together.

00:03:33.545 --> 00:03:35.848
I think it was important to do.

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:38.550
And I'm having a lot of fun,
man.

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:41.454
-I think it's important for you
to keep doing stuff like that.

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:43.255
I love that you keep doing stuff
like that.

00:03:43.255 --> 00:03:45.791
Let's talk about your movie
"Without Remorse."

00:03:45.791 --> 00:03:48.461
Now, this is Tom Clancy.

00:03:48.461 --> 00:03:51.430
This is big shoes right here.

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:52.765
-Yes, sir.

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:54.800
-What made you
want to do this one?

00:03:54.800 --> 00:04:00.272
-To be honest, as a kid, I used
to play "Rainbow Six" a lot.

00:04:00.272 --> 00:04:02.007
Yeah!
-Wow!

00:04:02.007 --> 00:04:04.944
-As a gamer, I used to play
the video game a lot,

00:04:04.944 --> 00:04:07.113
and I've been a fan
of Tom Clancy

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:09.515
and his universe ever since.

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:12.952
So when I had the opportunity
to check out the script

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:15.521
and breathe some life into it

00:04:15.521 --> 00:04:17.957
and basically modernize it,

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:20.459
make it more of a reflection of
the world that we live in today,

00:04:20.459 --> 00:04:22.061
I kind of jumped
at the opportunity,

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:23.896
especially to do my own stunts.

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:25.898
You grow up watching
these types of movies.

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:27.500
You know what I mean?
You got Wesley Snipes

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:30.503
and Tom Cruise
and Michael Jai White

00:04:30.503 --> 00:04:32.438
and Jackie Chan who trained,

00:04:32.438 --> 00:04:34.240
you know what I'm saying,
for these stunts.

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:35.708
And now I get a chance
to do it myself?

00:04:35.708 --> 00:04:37.176
I'm like, "Oh,
I'm all for that. Let me do it."

00:04:37.176 --> 00:04:39.145
-I watch you do
all these stunts.

00:04:39.145 --> 00:04:41.681
This really is
an action-packed movie.

00:04:41.681 --> 00:04:44.450
Like, beyond
action-packed movie.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:48.854
At one point, you're
fighting off three guys.

00:04:48.854 --> 00:04:50.757
You light a car on fire.

00:04:50.757 --> 00:04:52.858
And then you get in that car,
and I go,

00:04:52.858 --> 00:04:55.260
"Never seen that one before.
Wow!"

00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:59.198
And it's you doing it for real.
-Yeah, yeah. Yeah, that's me.

00:04:59.198 --> 00:05:02.534
-Are you afraid? See, I would be
afraid of messing up the take

00:05:02.534 --> 00:05:04.336
and be like, "Okay,
Jimmy, no big deal.

00:05:04.336 --> 00:05:06.639
We'll just light another car
on fire."

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:10.342
-It's one of those things that

00:05:10.342 --> 00:05:13.612
most of the stunts in the movie
you can train for.

00:05:13.612 --> 00:05:16.282
You can't really train yourself
not to be hot.

00:05:16.282 --> 00:05:18.217
You know what I'm saying?
The fire is the fire.

00:05:18.217 --> 00:05:20.186
So that was probably
the one stunt

00:05:20.186 --> 00:05:22.088
that I didn't think about
as much.

00:05:22.088 --> 00:05:23.256
I just wanted to do it.

00:05:23.256 --> 00:05:25.924
So they cover you
in this flame-retardant gel.

00:05:25.924 --> 00:05:27.159
You know what I mean?

00:05:27.159 --> 00:05:30.362
You might lose some eyebrows
and some eyelashes

00:05:30.362 --> 00:05:31.764
in the process.

00:05:31.764 --> 00:05:33.966
But I came away
with most of mine.

00:05:33.966 --> 00:05:35.567
You just kind of hop in the --

00:05:35.567 --> 00:05:39.204
you just hop in the car, man,
and you do the scene.

00:05:39.204 --> 00:05:41.073
And, you know,
you got to get out.

00:05:41.073 --> 00:05:43.376
It was hot. It was hot.
-Yeah.

00:05:43.376 --> 00:05:46.612
Dude, this is fantastic.
And congrats on this one.

00:05:46.612 --> 00:05:48.514
I want everyone to take a look
at this. Here's a clip.

00:05:48.514 --> 00:05:51.383
Here's Michael B. Jordan
in "Without Remorse."

00:05:51.383 --> 00:05:57.557
♪♪

00:05:57.557 --> 00:06:00.626
-You remember me? Huh? Who was
the fourth guy in my house?

00:06:00.626 --> 00:06:02.528
Give me a name.

00:06:02.528 --> 00:06:04.263
-Aah!

00:06:04.263 --> 00:06:06.299
-You give me a name.

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:09.702
-Aah!

00:06:11.137 --> 00:06:14.374
Okay. I'll give you a name.

00:06:16.976 --> 00:06:18.877
John Kelly.

00:06:18.877 --> 00:06:22.048
You're problem.

00:06:22.048 --> 00:06:24.383
You're supposed to be dead.

00:06:24.383 --> 00:06:26.452
-Wow!

00:06:26.452 --> 00:06:29.121
That's how you do it, buddy.
Michael B. Jordan, everybody.

00:06:29.121 --> 00:06:33.126
"Without Remorse" is available
on Amazon Prime Video tomorrow.

